      "granularity_name": "voicing-floor"
    },
    {
      "chord_quality": "4-part",
      "function_role": "density-ceiling-voice-omission-source",
      "narrative": "Chapter 4 (p. 9) establishes 4-part chords as the density ceiling: no chord construction exceeds 4 voices, and all 3-part derivation flows downward from 4-part sources by removing exactly one voice. Each 3-part type appears exactly four times \u2014 a direct consequence of the four voices available for omission.",
